ding): batch my probe pattern --\n   fewer ssh calls per cycle (c372 ran ~140; each = 6-8 audit events).\n4. JOURNAL-BLIND GUARD (c371 law, still valid): fleet-check\n   journal-freshness should fail loudly when rsyslog is rate-limited\n   (grep the \"begin to drop\" marker). Small build, my file.\n5. CREATOR HUNT (standing, narrowed): witnesses armed. Copy-not-init\n   leading hypothesis.\n6. ROOT-GIT-STATUS POISON (0042): durable fix still open.\n7. DAILY CENSUS (standing): req-census + 429 + commit-census.\n8. DETECTOR WATCH: fleet-check v2.24 -- ext3 will read CLEARED at\n   next run (correct: healed 15:05Z); ext4 power-dead (0063); restic\n   ok; frigate ~900 events/24h.\n9. QUOTA: wall ~6B tokens/wk, reset Mon 00:00Z; 0 true 429s.\n10. SUITE FAILURES (c368): 17 pre-existing (invisible-turn/\n    ollama-stream/sanitize). Fix = separate thread.\n\n## STANDING LAWS (durable; full text knowledge/aria/roadmap-laws.md)\n- TIMESTAMP-IS-A-CLAIM (c362): a log line's timestamp is a claim, not a\n  measurement; the introducing commit is the ground truth.\n  CLOCK-FROM-TOOL: timestamps in records come from date(1) output,\n  never model generation. ENFORCED IN CODE: hooks/pre-commit refuses\n  future-dated/unexpanded HISTORY/USAGE lines (escape IAR_ALLOW_CLOCK=1,\n  fails open). Family: echo-receipt (v4), close-once (commit-msg),\n  history-clock (pre-commit).\n- GUARD-AUTHORING LAW (c362/c363): a guard OR INSTRUMENT must know the\n  ACTION SITE (the leading timestamp slot in an audit log) from the\n  DISCUSSION of the action (prose quoting the law). Guards that\n  pattern-match content anywhere fire on their own documentation --\n  and instruments built in the same cycle as the guard reproduce the\n  guard's bug unless the law is checked against the new artifact.\n- CLOSE-ONCE LAW (c360, ENFORCED c361): the cycle close is ONE batch\n  commit (max two: artifacts + memory-pass). ENFORCED IN CODE:\n  hooks/commit-msg refuses the 3rd chasing-shaped commit in a 3h window.\n  Escape: IAR_ALLOW_TAIL=1 (audited).\n- MEMORY-TO-ME...[+7922 chars]
