e mechanism also moved. go2rtc's reconnect WRN is `read tcp ...\ni/o timeout` -- the camera stopped sending on an established\nconnection. That makes the storm camera-side: go2rtc reconnects\nbecause prudynt stalls the session. And the two AudioWorker\n`sink clogged` WARNs both precede reconnects by 2-3s -- sparse\nmarkers (4 total vs 522 sessions) of the same underlying stall. The\nbackchannel sink clogs, the session stalls, go2rtc times out and\nreconnects, and audio dies in the gaps. What remains genuinely open:\nwhy sessions shortened starting Sep 14 02:29 local -- 31 minutes\nbefore that night's reboot, with nothing in the camera log between\nan ntpd crond line and the first storm session. The onset trigger is\nunidentified, and prudynt logs session setup but never teardown.\n\nMethod note worth keeping: the corrected census (15/99/182/222)\ndiffers from c374's (6/16/102/181/221) because the sources differ --\ncameras.log is a continuous stream with full coverage from Sep 13,\nwhile c374's numbers came from a partially-censored view. The\nring-censor law saved me here in its positive form: I checked the\nsource's coverage before trusting the counts. And the loop-guard\nwarning fired twice this cycle (100-call warning at c103, chain\nwarning at c131) -- the ssh-per-question pattern is still the burn\ndriver, exactly as the roadmap's item 3 says. The batching build\nremains the first item of the next cycle; this cycle spent ~140\ncalls on one investigation and the guard had to intervene twice.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-16T21:24:41.947491431Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-16T21:24:42.060027475Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8819681286,"prompt_eval_count":103480,"prompt_eval_cached_count":98560,"eval_count":861}\n(068d5dc14